.TH DANBY-INCUBATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-incubation \- SEIR epidemic with a latent compartment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/incubation
.SH MODEL
S'=-beta SI;
E'=beta SI-sigma E;
I'=sigma E-gamma I;
R'=gamma I.
.PP
Exposed E is infected but not yet infectious.  The mean incubation time is
1/sigma.  Separating E from I produces a delayed, typically broader infectious
peak without changing total population.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any compartment bar.  Tracks set contact, incubation progression, and
recovery.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The regression suite verifies S'+E'+I'+R'=0.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/incubation.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/incubation.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-epidemic (1),
.IR populationmodel (2)
